  "_comment": "Scenario ABC (Notion: 시나리오 ABC, section 7). Times are simulation seconds, SAGAT freezes excluded. Lanes as in the document: 1 = left of the ego car, 2 = the ego car's lane, 3 = right of it. On Town04 they are the real highway lanes 2, 3 and 4 (real lane 1, next to the median, stays empty). Q and F times are fixed here; make_schedule.py builds the background traffic so that each Q's target layout happens by itself at its time. TOR (Notion, 2026-11-09, again): once per block and in the practice drive, at the end. Its \"t\" in the sets is the target; abc_schedule.py moves it (at most move_max_s) onto a straight (straight_rel_s around it), at least after_window_s after the last gaze window, tor_apart_s apart in A, B, C. The background traffic is gone from clear_rel_s on; the block ends end_rel_s after the TOR (5 s after the car stands still). blocks.*.block_end_s is only how far ahead the curves are looked at; the schedule's block_end_s is TOR + end_rel_s.",
